{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785993791663632001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"blank-clout-greed","assignee":"","attestations":{"plan-review":{"algorithm":"HMAC-SHA256","author":"Joe Oakhart","head_sha":"a06d00a95936e63d198de7279b767a039c889147","key_id":"412fa5372ad877e0","kind":"plan-review","manifest":["plan-review: PASS","ticket: 7522-129b-1380-418c","material: d5c4e1bc086d3070","model: claude-sonnet-4-6","runner: pydantic_ai","blocking: 0","advisory: 11","rebar-version: 0.6.0 (a06d00a95-dirty)","regver: bb57585159a067c5","verified-at-sha:c12ad713bcdbbccda4451e43585d09eb01d14583","dep absent src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py"],"signature":"bed02103e0a60043c5b02e315389ecb15b4f56bc8119f7ff00e70c65b8686a48","signed_at":1783232146126873000}},"author":"Joe Oakhart","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":13},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1783216079196182001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b1ac21ca-0a52-4367-b1cb-c2f4dd5dc4e4","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"524d-00fa-66ef-4432"}],"description":"## What\n\nAdd **lease-based self-healing** on top of the C1 ref-lock primitive so a crashed pass-holder\nnever wedges the reconciler beyond one lease interval. Builds directly on C1.\n\n**Depends on: 524d-00fa-66ef-4432 (C1).** C1 delivers the `_ref_lock.py` module, the blob schema\n(`heartbeat_ns`, `fence`), the `acquire`/`release`/`read` API, and the CAS helpers. **This child\nADDS `renew()` plus the lease-expiry/steal logic to that module** — it is not standalone and C1\nmust be merged first. (`renew()` is introduced here, not in C1.)\n\n- **Relative-duration, skew-proof lease (DynamoDB-lock-client pattern):** expiry is NOT a\n  cross-clone timestamp comparison. A contender records `(observed_oid, fence)`, waits one lease\n  interval measured on its **own** clock, re-reads; if `fence` and the ref oid are unchanged, the\n  holder made no progress for a full lease -> considered dead. This is why the stored `heartbeat_ns`\n  is only diagnostic and the design is skew-proof.\n- **`renew()`** (heartbeat) CAS-updates the blob's `heartbeat_ns` and increments `fence`\n  (`fence += 1`) while the holder still owns the ref (old = observed oid). `fence` is a **monotonic\n  progress-witness / generation counter** — it is the signal the expiry rule reads; it is NOT a\n  full fencing token handed to the protected resource (no stale-writer rejection is claimed).\n- **CAS-break-on-expiry:** a contender may steal **only** an expired lease, by CAS-replacing the\n  blob against the exact observed OID. Because the steal is a compare-and-swap on the observed oid,\n  a **double-break race resolves to exactly one winner** — the loser's CAS fails, it backs off and\n  does NOT also acquire.\n- **Lease + cadence config:** default lease **120 s**, heartbeat interval **`max(1, lease // 3)`**\n  seconds (integer floor, not a vague `~lease/3`), read from a new `[reconciler]` key\n  `lock_lease_secs`. Registering that key is C3's job (the `_config_schema.py` wiring lands with the\n  `lock_backend` switch); here it is consumed with a safe default so C2 is testable standalone.\n- **`renew()` failure contract:** a rejected renewal CAS means the lease was lost/stolen. `renew()`\n  raises a **named exception** (e.g. `LeaseLostError`) — it does NOT silently retry into another\n  holder's lock. The orchestrator (C3) turns that exception into a pass-abort.\n- Structured log emission for lease-steal, renewal-failure, and expiry-detection events.\n- Lives in `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py` (extends C1); no reconciler\n  orchestration wiring (that is C3). Extend the C1 ADR with the lease/heartbeat/fence contract.\n\n## Design decisions (resolves plan-review ambiguities; binding on the implementation)\n\n1. **API surface added to `_ref_lock.py`.** `renew(repo_root, ref, *, oid, remote=None) -> str`;\n   and the steal is split into a **testable core** `try_break_if_stale(repo_root, ref, *, first,\n   holder, remote=None) -> str | None` plus a convenience `steal(repo_root, ref, *, holder,\n   remote=None, sleep_fn=time.sleep) -> str | None` that does observe -> `sleep_fn(first.lease_secs)`\n   -> `try_break_if_stale`. The one-lease wait is injected via `sleep_fn` so unit tests exercise the\n   CAS/expiry logic **without real time**; a short configured lease also keeps any live test fast.\n2. **`renew()` contract.** Reads the current state; if the ref is absent or no longer points at\n   `oid` -> `LeaseLostError` (no CAS attempted). Otherwise it CAS-updates the blob to\n   `{holder, lease_secs (unchanged), heartbeat_ns=time.time_ns(), fence+1}` against `oid` (via the\n   shared `_cas_once` seam / `--force-with-lease` on the remote path); a rejected CAS ->\n   `LeaseLostError`. Returns the new oid the caller threads into the next `renew`. It NEVER retries\n   into another holder's lock.\n3. **Steal contract.** `try_break_if_stale` takes the `first` observation and re-reads: if the ref\n   is now free (`None`) or its `(oid, fence)` changed -> returns `None` (the holder released or made\n   progress = live, never stolen). Otherwise it CAS-replaces the blob against `first.oid` with\n   `{holder=<contender>, lease_secs=first.lease_secs, heartbeat_ns=now, fence=first.fence + 1}`; a\n   rejected CAS (lost the single-winner race) -> `None`. It never steals a **free** ref (that is\n   `acquire`) and never steals a **live/renewing** holder.\n4. **Fail-closed during steal/renew.** A `RefLockCorruptError` / `RefLockTimeoutError` from any read\n   in the steal/renew path propagates (fail-closed = treat as HELD); a contender never steals on an\n   unreadable blob.\n5. **Lease constants.** `DEFAULT_LEASE_SECS = 120` and `heartbeat_interval(lease) -> max(1,\n   int(lease // 3))` live in `_ref_lock.py`; C3 wires `[reconciler] lock_lease_secs` into the\n   `acquire` call. `lease_secs` is carried IN the blob, so a contender waits the **holder's** lease,\n   not its own — the skew-proof relative-duration rule.\n6. **Structured logs.** Emit on lease-steal (won a break), expiry-detection (no `(oid, fence)`\n   progress across one lease), and renewal-failure (`LeaseLostError`).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `_ref_lock.py` gains `renew()` (owner-only CAS-update of `heartbeat_ns`, `fence += 1`, against\n      the held oid) and a lease-expiry evaluation using observed-no-progress-over-one-locally-measured\n      -lease, not an absolute cross-clone clock diff; `renew()` on a lost/stolen lease raises\n      `LeaseLostError` (no silent retry) and returns the new oid on success.\n- [ ] A contender CAS-breaks only an expired lease (no `fence`/oid progress across one lease); a\n      live, heartbeating holder is never stolen from (regression test); a free ref is never \"stolen\"\n      (that path is `acquire`).\n- [ ] Double-break race: two contenders race to steal one expired lock (both call\n      `try_break_if_stale` against the same `first`); exactly one wins, the other observes CAS\n      failure and returns `None` (does NOT acquire) — single-winner regression test.\n- [ ] Lease = `[reconciler] lock_lease_secs` (default `DEFAULT_LEASE_SECS = 120`), heartbeat interval\n      `heartbeat_interval(lease) = max(1, lease // 3)`, not hardcoded at the call sites; the one-lease\n      wait is injectable (`sleep_fn`) so tests need no real sleep.\n- [ ] A corrupt/unreadable blob encountered during steal/renew fails closed (treated as HELD), never\n      stolen.\n- [ ] Lease-steal / renewal-failure / expiry-detection events emit structured logs; the C1 ADR is\n      extended with the lease/heartbeat/fence contract. Non-integration suite green.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py","reason":"lease/heartbeat/CAS-break self-heal"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","524d-00fa-66ef-4432"],["parent","6c9c-811f-6dc4-40e7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"6c9c-811f-6dc4-40e7","parent_status_uuid":"89f95db2-750a-450c-8ab6-a6789dff9e2d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"7522-129b-1380-418c","ticket_type":"task","title":"Lease + heartbeat + CAS-break-on-stale self-healing (single-winner)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e68aee92-a517-4478-8d99-b67ec3c89187","b1ac21ca-0a52-4367-b1cb-c2f4dd5dc4e4","dfb9e92c-3c8b-49d8-82f4-df8194b07a5a","7c386416-5c85-445f-9281-606c09480649","c4d8d8dc-1fdd-4ce1-b0c5-45b87576d981","5b9ffe74-a925-473a-b70c-2d9fa6dc15df","14438135-6a2e-442a-bcff-d7efa53c0d35","5e388a70-28e2-4d0d-ac94-e5039b00d128","4b68772d-169a-4440-bcaf-e951de687253","28ee8a05-e4ee-4823-924e-72cdef00eac9","34e85447-36e3-4594-93bc-69b0d798edcf","dc2bfa06-9c8c-4354-8c05-05dd00c4b13f","775ca51e-75fc-4c88-a55d-289a771c1c9b","0ce9a840-989b-40f7-902d-45f4c4cbb449","89f95db2-750a-450c-8ab6-a6789dff9e2d","f0ab4cab-eacc-4895-b979-1b669f078c59","c0a4a8c4-c1c2-4e4a-895f-11a8b96bd2c5","100ae38e-5177-4b95-ae77-5325e1cfb96d"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785993791663632001,"uuid":"6d0a304a-5a6f-4012-a51b-7f2963e51d61"}